---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@/config/site';
---

<LegalLayout path="/terms-of-service/" heading="Terms of Service" updated={new Date('2026-10-12')}>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of <a href="/">hiver.com.np</a>, operated by {site.name},
    {site.address.display}. By using the site you agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use
    the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Services and products</h2>
  <p>
    Information on this site describes our services and products in general terms. It is not an offer.
    Any engagement is governed by a separate written agreement, statement of work or licence, which
    takes precedence over these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of the site</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the site lawfully and do not attempt to disrupt, overload or gain unauthorized access to it.</li>
    <li>Do not submit false, misleading or automated enquiries.</li>
    <li>Do not copy substantial parts of the site for commercial use without permission.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Unless stated otherwise, the content, design and branding on this site belong to {site.name}.
    Third-party names and logos remain the property of their owners and are used only to identify
    technologies we work with. Ownership of client work is defined in each client agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy and availability</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to keep information accurate and current, but the site is provided “as is”. Guides and
    articles are general information, not professional advice for your specific situation. We may
    change or withdraw content without notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss arising from
    use of the site. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>We are not responsible for the content or practices of websites we link to.</p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Nepal, and the courts of Nepal have jurisdiction.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
